participant User
participant "<color:#white>Mobile App (Core ทางรัฐ)</color>" as CoreApp #2E7D32
participant "<color:#white>Document Wallet (Miniapp)</color>" as Mini #2E7D32
participant "<color:#white>DW Core</color>" as DW #steelblue
participant "Verifier Officer" as Officer
participant "<color:#white>Verifier Toolkit</color>" as VSys #6A1B9A
participant "<color:#white>VCVP Core</color>" as Core #3F51B5
participant "<color:#white>one-core (VP Engine)</color>" as VPEngine #chocolate
participant "<color:#white>one-core (VC Engine)</color>" as VCEngine #chocolate
participant "<color:#white>HSM (AWS KMS)</color>" as HSM #darkgoldenrod
participant "<color:#white>ETDA Trusted List (CDN)</color>" as Trust #0B2E6B

note over DW,Trust #violet: 0. Load ETDA Trusted Lists (when a transaction needs them)
note right of DW #wheat:[CONDITION] before this flow (setup , outside the system) : the verifier is registered in ver.txt (VP part 0)\nand DW Core in wp.txt as wallet provider
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] steps in the ETDA Trusted List Load sequence (first tab) | DW Core loads ver.txt (section 1.2) , VCVP Core loads wp.txt (section 7.1) and iss.txt (section 7.2)
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• appendix 8.2 E.1.1 (MUST)  the wallet fetches the ETDA key and ver.txt
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Trusted List not usable (TRUST_LIST_EXPIRED / TRUST_LIST_UNAVAILABLE) : the calling step answers 503 Service Unavailable + Retry-After: 300\nnot the trust failure reason of that step , as in the ETDA Trusted List Load sequence

note right of Mini #wheat:[SPEC] The verification link reaches the wallet by QR or deep link\nVCVP and DW Core do not push the link to the app
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Protocol endpoints (/ssi) carry no Consumer-Key\nrequest object and response write VCVPAuditLog (Actor Channel = WALLET , no caller OrgCode)
User->Mini: Scan QR / open deep link

note over Mini,HSM #lightblue: 1. DW Core fetches the request object and checks the verifier for the app (/dw/v1/presentation/start)
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 13.4 (MUST NOT)  sensitive elements not routed through a server component that is not fully trusted
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core is the server component of the wallet and is declared a fully trusted part of it (VCVP design decision)\nthe app calls only DW Core , DW Core makes every protocol call , the app signs and encrypts , DW Core checks the verifier (TC-1) for the wallet
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 15.1 (SHOULD NOT)  transaction history accessible to others\n• 15.2 (SHOULD)  privacy notice available
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core sees the verifier , the time and the requested claims in the request object , never the VP\nthis is stated in the privacy notice of the wallet
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core policy : URLs from a QR are called only over https and never to internal addresses
Mini->DW: Start verification + Token | POST /dw/v1/presentation/start (DW endpoint 12)\n(QR or deep link content)
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 5.1 (MUST)  no request_uri_method , GET as in RFC 9101
DW->DW: Validate Token → CitizenId\nParse openid4vp:// → client_id , request_uri
DW->Core: Read request object from request_uri | GET /ssi/openid4vp/final-1.0/{id}/client-request (VCVP Core 26)
Core->VPEngine: Read request object | GET /ssi/openid4vp/final-1.0/{id}/client-request
note over VPEngine,HSM #f4cccc: 1.1 Verifier signs the request object (signing point 1)
note right of VPEngine #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] signed with the verifier DID key in AWS KMS , kid in the JOSE header = verificationMethod id of that key\nno verifier attestation (client_id prefix decentralized_identifier)\nThe engine signs again each time the request object is read (nonce stays the same)
VPEngine->HSM: Sign request object (JWS ES256) with the verifier key
HSM-->VPEngine: Signature
note right of VPEngine #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 5 (MUST NOT)  no request object without typ = oauth-authz-req+jwt\n• 5.1  dcql_query\n• 5.2 (REQUIRED)  nonce , response_mode\n• 5.8  aud of a request object\n• 8.2 (REQUIRED)  response_uri\n• 8.3.1  response mode direct_post.jwt
note right of VPEngine #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] request object of the engine\nheader : typ = oauth-authz-req+jwt , alg = ES256 , kid = verifier DID verificationMethod\npayload : client_id = decentralized_identifier:{verifier DID} , nonce , state , response_type = vp_token\nresponse_mode = direct_post.jwt , response_uri , dcql_query , client_metadata (jwks , vp_formats_supported ,\nencrypted_response_enc_values_supported)
VPEngine-->Core: Request object (JWT , application/oauth-authz-req+jwt)
note right of Core #wheat:[DATA STORE] used to find this request when the wallet asks for verifier information or cancels
Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store state and nonce of the request object in Verifications table\n(state = engine interaction id → InteractionId)
Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of /ssi client-request (EngineCalls , Correlation.VerificationId)
DW<--Core: Request object (signed JWT)
DW->DW: Read kid from the JOSE header of the request object (the verifier DID before #)
DW->Core: Get verifier DID document | GET /ssi/did-web/v1/{id}/did.json (VCVP Core 17)
Core->VPEngine: Get verifier DID document | GET /ssi/did-web/v1/{id}/did.json
VPEngine-->Core: DID document | verificationMethod[] { id , publicKeyJwk }
DW<--Core: DID document

note over DW,Trust #violet: 1.2 DW Core checks the verifier for the wallet (TC-1)
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• appendix 8.2 E.1.5 (MUST)  TC-1 passes before any data is sent\n• 8.4.1 step 3 (MUST)  verifier service found by ServiceTypeIdentifier and key , organisation and service status active
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core runs TC-1 for the wallet before it answers the app , the app receives only the result and the request values
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 5 (MUST NOT)  no request object without typ = oauth-authz-req+jwt
DW->DW: Check typ = oauth-authz-req+jwt in the JOSE header
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 8.1.2 (MUST)  client identifier prefix from OpenID4VP , decentralized_identifier allowed\n• 12.7  x509_san_dns listed for verifiers in the Trusted List\n• chapter 14 SC-09  the wallet enforces the client_id prefix\n• 12.2.1 (MUST NOT)  no redirect_uri client_id without a DID
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 5.10.1 (MUST)  client_id of the QR and of the request object identical , including the prefix\n• 15.8.1 (SHOULD)  the request_uri belongs to the client_id
DW->DW: Check client_id from the QR = client_id in the request object (with the decentralized_identifier: prefix)\nCheck the host of request_uri and response_uri = the host of the verifier did:web
DW->DW: Read verifier DID = client_id without the decentralized_identifier: prefix , read kid\nLook up the verifier DID in the Verifier Trusted List (L2) : service type = verifier (ServiceTypeIdentifier) , listed keys , organisation and service status = active , validity period current
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 5.9.3 (MUST)  decentralized_identifier , the key comes from the verificationMethod identified by kid\nThai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 12.6 (MUST NOT)  no DID document key instead of the Trusted List key
DW->DW: Find the verificationMethod whose id = kid , the DID in kid = the verifier DID\nthe public key MUST equal a key listed for the verifier in the Trusted List
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 5.8 (MUST)  aud of the request object = https://self-issued.me/v2 with static discovery
note right of DW #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : appendix 8.2 E.1.5 writes aud = wallet ID , OpenID4VP 1.0 section 5.8 uses https://self-issued.me/v2\nquestion : which aud value must the request object carry
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] RFC 7515\n• 5.2  JWS signature validation
DW->DW: Verify the request object signature (JWS) , reject alg none\nCheck aud , exp and iat , nonce length at least 128 bits
note right of DW #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : appendix 8.2 E.1.5 (MUST) the wallet rejects a request whose purpose cannot be checked , the engine request object has no purpose field and the Thai profile has not defined one\nquestion : which field carries the purpose (OpenID4VP 1.0 section 5.11 verifier_info (OPTIONAL) could carry a signed purpose)
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] VCVP Core gives the purpose to the wallet through DW Core (section 2) until ETDA defines the field
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] decided by ETDA after discussion : checking the requested claims and the purpose against ver.txt is phase 2 work , not done in phase 1
DW->DW: Check the requested claims (dcql_query.credentials[].claims[].path) and the purpose\nare within the scope allowed for this verifier in the Trusted List

alt Request object invalid / verifier not in the Trusted List / request outside the verifier scope
    note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• appendix 8.2 E.1.5 (MUST)  TC-1 fails , stop at once and send nothing
    note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core records the reason only , VCVP Core is not called , the request expires at the verifier
    DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store presentation request in DW database\n(state , CitizenId , Status = REQUEST_INVALID / VERIFIER_NOT_TRUSTED , no claim values)
    DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (reason = REQUEST_INVALID / VERIFIER_NOT_TRUSTED)
    Mini<--DW: 200 (response of /dw/v1/presentation/start) | verifierTrust = NOT_TRUSTED , reason = REQUEST_INVALID / VERIFIER_NOT_TRUSTED
    Mini-->User: Verification request rejected\nVerifier is not trusted
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Flow stops here , the verifier sees the request expire (no reason is sent to the verifier side)
else Request object valid and verifier trusted
    Mini<--DW: 200 (response of /dw/v1/presentation/start) | verifierTrust = TRUSTED , client_id , state , nonce , response_uri ,\nclient_metadata.jwks + encrypted_response_enc_values_supported , dcql_query
    note right of Mini #wheat:[SPEC] Keep nonce , client_id (→ section 6)\nKeep state , response_uri , client_metadata.jwks + encrypted_response_enc_values_supported (→ section 7)\nKeep dcql_query (→ section 3)
    Mini->Mini: Keep the request values for the next sections

end

note over Mini,Core #violet: 2. Wallet gets the verifier details for the consent screen
Mini->DW: Get verifier information + Token | POST /dw/v1/presentation/info (DW endpoint 13)\n(state from request object)
DW->DW: Validate Token → CitizenId\n[DATA STORE] Store presentation request in DW database (state , CitizenId , Status = PENDING)
DW->Core: Get verifier information | POST /api/proof-request/v1/verifier-info (VCVP Core 27)\n(state)
Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) , otherwise 401 FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED / 403 FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Purpose and LegalBasis were stored when the verifier created the proof request
Core->Core: Find Verifications table by state , not found 403 FailureReason = VERIFICATION_NOT_FOUND\nRead verifier organisation , Purpose , LegalBasis
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 12.8 (MUST)  the Trusted List is fetched when the connection needs a trust decision
Core->Core: Look up the verifier in the Verifier Trusted List again (ver.txt , ETDA Trusted List Load)\nservice type = verifier (ServiceTypeIdentifier) , name (TEName) , organisation and service status = active , validity period current
alt Verifier no longer active in the Trusted List
    Core->Core: Update Verifications table Status = VERIFIER_NOT_TRUSTED\ndo not call the engine , let the request expire
    Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 27 (TrustCheck.Result = FAILED)
    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] verifier not trusted : verifier_trust.result = FAILED (result is PASSED or FAILED)
    DW<--Core: 200 | verifier_trust
    Mini<--DW: Reject verification request
    Mini-->User: Verification cancelled\nVerifier is not trusted
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Flow stops here , the verifier sees VERIFIER_NOT_TRUSTED in section 9
else Verifier still active
    Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 27 (TrustCheck)
    note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• appendix 8.2 E.1.6  consent screen shows the verifier legal_name from the Trusted List and the purpose\n• chapter 14 SC-08  the UI shows the name from the Trusted List only
    DW<--Core: 200 | verifier_name_en , verifier_name_local , org_code , purpose (code , text , legal_basis) , verifier_trust
    Mini<--DW: verifier details

end

note over CoreApp #lightblue: 3. Wallet matches the request with stored credentials (DCQL)
note right of CoreApp #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 5 (MUST)  the wallet processes the DCQL query (6.4)\n• 6  DCQL\nThai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• appendix 8.2 E.1.6  DCQL match
Mini->CoreApp: Find credentials that match dcql_query
note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] format = dc+sd-jwt , vct in meta.vct_values , every requested claim path present ,\ncnf bound to this device key (require_cryptographic_holder_binding = true) , evaluate credential_sets
CoreApp->CoreApp: Search the on-device database

alt No matching credential
    CoreApp-->Mini: No matching credential
    Mini->DW: Report presentation result + Token | POST /dw/v1/presentation/result (DW endpoint 15)\n(result = DECLINED , reason = NO_MATCHING_CREDENTIAL)
    note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 8.5  access_denied covers no matching credential , no consent and failed user authentication\n• 15.9 (SHOULD)  errors do not let the verifier infer user data
    note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] the verifier side only sees HOLDER_DECLINED
    DW->DW: Keep the detailed reason in the DW sharing confirmation record , send reason = HOLDER_DECLINED to VCVP Core
    DW->Core: Holder ends the verification request before sending VP | POST /api/proof-request/v1/cancel (VCVP Core 28)\nstate , reason
    Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) , otherwise 401 FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED / 403 FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] VCVP Core records the decline itself and does not call the engine , the request expires in the engine\nOpenID4VP 1.0 8.5 has the wallet send error = access_denied to response_uri , engine 1.89.3 accepts only vp_token or response (JWE)\nremove when the engine accepts the 8.5 error response and updates the proof request state itself
    Core->Core: Find Verifications table by state (InteractionId) , not found 403 FailureReason = VERIFICATION_NOT_FOUND\nStatus not PENDING : 409 FailureReason = VERIFICATION_ALREADY_ENDED , status not overwritten\nreason not in CancelReason (HOLDER_DECLINED , REQUEST_EXPIRED) : 400 FailureReason = REQUEST_REJECTED\nUpdate Status = REJECTED (Reason sent = HOLDER_DECLINED)
    Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 28 : the holder ended the request (EventType = VERIFICATION_CANCELLED , Reason = HOLDER_DECLINED , Correlation.VerificationId)
    DW<--Core: 200
    Mini<--DW: 200
    Mini-->User: No matching credential
else Matching credential found
    Mini->Mini: Continue to holder consent (section 4)
end

note over User,Mini #lightblue: 4. Holder reviews and consents
note right of Mini #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 8.6 , 8.8 (MUST)  consent UI shows the verifier , the requested data and the purpose\n• appendix 8.2 E.1.6  consent screen content\n• chapter 14 SC-08  names from the Trusted List only\nOpenID4VP 1.0\n• 15.1 (SHOULD)  explicit , informed consent
note right of Mini #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : the sample Trusted Lists have TEName and ServiceName in English only , no Thai name , no legal_name field (appendix 8.2 E.1.6) and no logo (section 13.7.1)\nquestion : which name does the consent screen show (TEName or ServiceName)
Mini-->User: Show verifier name (TEName from the Verifier Trusted List checked in 1.2) , trust result , purpose , legal basis\nrequested claims , claims to disclose
User->Mini: Accept / Reject

alt User rejects
    Mini->Mini: [AUDIT LOG] Store sharing confirmation record on device (REJECTED , verifier , requested claim names , timestamp)
    Mini->DW: Report presentation result + Token | POST /dw/v1/presentation/result (DW endpoint 15)\n(result = DECLINED , reason = USER_DENIED_CONSENT)
    DW->DW: Keep the detailed reason in the DW sharing confirmation record , send reason = HOLDER_DECLINED to VCVP Core
    DW->Core: Holder ends the verification request before sending VP | POST /api/proof-request/v1/cancel (VCVP Core 28)\nstate , reason
    Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) , otherwise 401 FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED / 403 FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 8.5  access_denied error sent to response_uri
    note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] VCVP Core records the decline itself and does not call the engine , the request expires in the engine\nOpenID4VP 1.0 8.5 has the wallet send error = access_denied to response_uri , engine 1.89.3 accepts only vp_token or response (JWE)\nremove when the engine accepts the 8.5 error response and updates the proof request state itself
    Core->Core: Find Verifications table by state (InteractionId) , not found 403 FailureReason = VERIFICATION_NOT_FOUND\nStatus not PENDING : 409 FailureReason = VERIFICATION_ALREADY_ENDED , status not overwritten\nreason not in CancelReason (HOLDER_DECLINED , REQUEST_EXPIRED) : 400 FailureReason = REQUEST_REJECTED\nUpdate Status = REJECTED (Reason sent = HOLDER_DECLINED)
    Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 28 : the holder ended the request (EventType = VERIFICATION_CANCELLED , Reason = HOLDER_DECLINED , Correlation.VerificationId)
    DW<--Core: 200
    Mini<--DW: 200
    Mini-->User: Sharing cancelled
else User accepts
    User->Mini: Confirm with biometric / PIN (unlocks the holder key and the instance key)
    Mini->Mini: [AUDIT LOG] Store sharing confirmation record on device (ACCEPTED , verifier , selected claim names , timestamp)

end

note over CoreApp #lightblue: 5. Wallet loads the credential
CoreApp->CoreApp: Load the full token (SD_JWT_VC + disclosures) from the on-device database

note over CoreApp #f4cccc: 6. Wallet builds the presentation , KB-JWT and WIA-PoP (signing point 2)
note right of CoreApp #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• appendix 8.2 E.1.7 (MUST)  a government wallet creates WIA-PoP\nOpenID4VP 1.0\n• Appendix B.3.6 (MUST)  KB-JWT nonce and aud\nRFC 9901 (SD-JWT)\n• 4.3 (MUST)  sd_hash over issuer JWT ~ disclosures ~
note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] KB-JWT typ = kb+jwt , signed with the holder key
CoreApp->CoreApp: Keep only the disclosures of the consented claims\nAssemble [issuer SD-JWT] ~ [selected disclosures] ~ and compute sd_hash
CoreApp->CoreApp: Sign KB-JWT with the holder key (Secure Enclave / Android Keystore / StrongBox)\nnonce , aud = client_id (full value with the decentralized_identifier: prefix) , iat , sd_hash
CoreApp->CoreApp: Create a new WIA key for this presentation , sign the WIA request proof with it (jwk in the header)\nsign the bearer of the attestation request with the instance key
note right of CoreApp #wheat:[STANDARD] draft-ietf-oauth-attestation-based-client-auth-07\n• 5.2 rule 3 (MUST)  the PoP is verified with the key in the cnf of the attestation\nOpenID4VCI 1.0\n• Appendix E  the sub of the Wallet Attestation is the client_id of the Wallet instance
note right of CoreApp #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : appendix 8.2 E.1.7 says WIA-PoP is signed with the "wallet instance key" and iss = "wallet instance ID"\nquestion : with a new WIA per presentation , is the WIA-PoP signed with the key in the WIA cnf and iss = the WIA sub
CoreApp->CoreApp: Sign WIA-PoP with the new WIA key\niss = WIA sub (wallet client id) , aud = client_id , nonce , jti , iat , exp
CoreApp->CoreApp: Build vp_token = { dcql credential id : [ issuer SD-JWT ~ disclosures ~ KB-JWT ] }
note right of CoreApp #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 8.3 (MUST)  JWE alg = alg of the chosen jwk , kid in the JWE header\n• 8.3.1  response mode direct_post.jwt
note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] alg ECDH-ES in the engine metadata , enc from encrypted_response_enc_values_supported (default A128GCM)
CoreApp->CoreApp: Encrypt { vp_token , state } as JWE (recipient key = client_metadata.jwks , JWE header kid = kid of that key)
note right of CoreApp #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• appendix 8.2 E.1.8  wallet_attestation and wallet_attestation_pop are parameters of the response , not inside vp_token
CoreApp-->Mini: response (JWE) + WIA request proof + bearer + WIA-PoP

alt Signing failed / key unavailable / user cancels
    Mini->DW: Report presentation result + Token | POST /dw/v1/presentation/result (DW endpoint 15)\n(result = FAILED , reason = SIGNING_FAILED / KEY_UNAVAILABLE / USER_CANCELLED)
    DW->DW: Keep the detailed reason in the DW sharing confirmation record , send reason = HOLDER_DECLINED to VCVP Core
    DW->Core: Holder ends the verification request before sending VP | POST /api/proof-request/v1/cancel (VCVP Core 28)\nstate , reason
    Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) , otherwise 401 FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED / 403 FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] VCVP Core records the decline itself and does not call the engine , the request expires in the engine\nOpenID4VP 1.0 8.5 has the wallet send error = access_denied to response_uri , engine 1.89.3 accepts only vp_token or response (JWE)\nremove when the engine accepts the 8.5 error response and updates the proof request state itself
    Core->Core: Find Verifications table by state (InteractionId) , not found 403 FailureReason = VERIFICATION_NOT_FOUND\nStatus not PENDING : 409 FailureReason = VERIFICATION_ALREADY_ENDED , status not overwritten\nreason not in CancelReason (HOLDER_DECLINED , REQUEST_EXPIRED) : 400 FailureReason = REQUEST_REJECTED\nUpdate Status = REJECTED (Reason sent = HOLDER_DECLINED)
    Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 28 : the holder ended the request (EventType = VERIFICATION_CANCELLED , Reason = HOLDER_DECLINED , Correlation.VerificationId)
    DW<--Core: 200
    Mini<--DW: 200
    Mini-->User: Sharing cancelled
else Presentation ready
    Mini->Mini: Continue to submit the presentation (section 7)
end

note over Mini,VPEngine #orange: 7. DW Core submits the presentation (/dw/v1/presentation/submit)
Mini->DW: Submit presentation + Token | POST /dw/v1/presentation/submit (DW endpoint 14)\n(state , response , WIA request proof , bearer , wallet_attestation_pop , disclosed claim names)
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] header x5c = wallet provider certificate (no iss) | cnf , wallet_name , wallet_version , wallet_solution_certification_information , wallet_link , client_status { status , exp }
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 10.3.2 (MUST NOT)  the verifier gets no device capability data\n• 10.5.1 (SHOULD)  WUA once-only or in a batch\nEUDI TS3 v1.5.2\n• 2.2.1.1 (SHALL)  WIA time-to-live less than 24 hours
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core puts no WSCD data in the WIA (eudi_wallet_info = null) , a new WIA with a new key for each presentation , valid 300 seconds
DW->DW: As the wallet provider : check wallet unit status = ACTIVE , the bearer with the registered instance key and the WIA request proof , sign a new WIA with the wallet provider key of DW\ncnf = the new WIA key , valid 300 seconds , client_status
alt Wallet unit revoked or the bearer or WIA request proof is invalid
    DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Update presentation request status = FAILED (reason = WALLET_ATTESTATION_FAILED , no claim values)
    Mini<--DW: 200 (response of /dw/v1/presentation/submit) | result = FAILED , reason = WALLET_ATTESTATION_FAILED
end
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\nresponse = JWE , wallet_attestation = the new WIA , wallet_attestation_pop = WIA-PoP
DW->Core: Submit presentation | POST /ssi/openid4vp/final-1.0/response (VCVP Core 29)
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 8.3  the response is encrypted to the verifier key in client_metadata.jwks
note right of HSM #wheat:[SPEC] the verifier keyAgreement key is one AWS KMS key (KeyUsage KEY_AGREEMENT , not exportable) , separate from the verifier signing key\nthe engine and VCVP Core use it through IAM permissions , there is no copy of the private key
note right of HSM #wheat:[STANDARD] NIST SP 800-57 Part 1 Rev. 5\n• 9.5.3.2  more copies of a key , more exposure
Core->HSM: Derive the shared secret | AWS KMS DeriveSharedSecret\n(verifier keyAgreement key , epk from the JWE header)
HSM-->Core: shared secret (ECDH)
Core->Core: Decrypt the response (Concat KDF , AES-GCM) : state and vp_token , no claim values are kept
Core->Core: Find the request in Verifications table : InteractionId = state from the decrypted response , read Nonce
alt Request not found
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 29 (FailureReason = VERIFICATION_NOT_FOUND)
    DW<--Core: 400 | error = invalid_request , vcvp_failure_reason = VERIFICATION_NOT_FOUND
    DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Update presentation request status = FAILED (reason = VERIFIER_REJECTED , no claim values)
    Mini<--DW: 200 (response of /dw/v1/presentation/submit) | result = FAILED , reason = VERIFIER_REJECTED
    Mini-->User: Sharing failed
else Request not PENDING
